From 76eba783d3a280c8107f1be375f9f4b37a438cfa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 07:21:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/15] perf(trafficcraft): skip packets of unchanged
 traffic-light updates

An unpowered traffic light calls setPowered(false) on every neighbour change
(redstone-triggered lights also stopSchedule), and schedules may re-enable
the colors already shown. DragonLib's notifyUpdate then queues a block update
and the full block-entity NBT for every tracking player. When the call leaves
its fields unchanged (colors compared object by object), keep setChanged for
chunk saving and comparators and skip only the redundant packets.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TD7PJ5R7t7hM3ymeeqXP4H
